---
source: crates/holst-cli/src/table.rs
expression: help_of(line)
---
Find boards by name and text on boards, the best match first.
It prints one line per match with @N and its link. Words match in any order; case and punctuation do not matter.

USAGE
  holst search <query> [flags]

ARGUMENTS
  query   Words to find, in any order

FLAGS
  -w, --workspace ws   Where names are looked up and new things go: a workspace id or part of its name; all of yours by default
      --mode mode      What to search: names, board-text or both; both by default
      --board board    Only this board: id, link or part of its name; reads board text
  -k, --kind kind      Only this kind: board, folder or any for names; sticker, text, shape, frame, arrow, image… for board text
      --trash          Also look in the trash
  -l, --limit n        At most this many matches; 0 shows all; 20 by default
      --refresh        Ignore the cached copy and download the board again
      --offline        No network: read the text of the --board, an id or link, from the cache, or fail when there is none

INHERITED FLAGS
  --output, --verbose, --base-url, --home, --no-cache, --help   as in `holst -h`

EXAMPLES
  $ holst search "retro"
  $ holst search "design" --mode board-text -w easy -k sticker
  $ holst search "Roadmap" --mode names -l 0

LEARN MORE
  How a board is given: `holst b -h`.
  Exit codes: `holst help exit-codes`.
